<body>
    <h1>User Creation in Polarion</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h3 id=3D"UserCreationinPolarion-1.1.1UserCreationinPolarion">1.1.1=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>User Creation in Polarion</u>=
</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <thead>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Who</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Does What</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>When</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>How</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Role / Access</p></td>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Cognizant AMS Team</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Process the User creation request in Polarion Production</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>When User requests access to Projects in Polarion Production</p></t=
d>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Cognizant AMS Team to follow the below steps to handle Polarion acc=
ess issues</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Role in Polarion Administration Tools Project in Production</p></td=
>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><strong><u>Actions</u></strong><u>: </u></p>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Cognizant AMS Team gets request=
s as per below different scenarios for User creation in Polarion Production=
.</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <stro=
ng><u>Scenario 1: New User Creation</u></strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>New Polarion user, who has never had access before, requests access in=
 Polarion Production server.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; The user raises a request in QuickSer=
vice portal under =E2=80=9CDigital User Account Request=E2=80=9D by clickin=
g on the link(see screenshot).</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-w=
rapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-i=
mage" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"350" src=3D"4e5c9148b5c47dc383335c41c559=
c5996d53bf8cf9eb81c20373f0f6fb5e529a" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachmen=
ts/78985264/image2021-9-15_4-56-33.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1=
631661995707&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-=
resource-id=3D"78987408" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-res=
ource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2021-9=
-15_4-56-33.png" data-base-url=3D"https://bluespace.fmeone.com" data-linked=
-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"7=
8985264" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"41" tabindex=3D"0" alt=
=3D"" height=3D"244"></span></p>
<ul>
 <li>The user fills the <span><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://qs=
ervice.intra.fmeone.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/create/283" rel=3D"n=
ofollow">Digital UACF</a></span> (there are different forms for Single User=
 creation and Multiple User creation). User also needs to attach the releva=
nt Training certificate as per the requested Roles.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wr=
apper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-im=
age" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"350" src=3D"02e780b48924342f1cc19f5277ec1=
f57b628f1f400cb70f3d02bcf763c8167c6" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachment=
s/78985264/image2021-9-15_4-56-53.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D16=
31662014956&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-r=
esource-id=3D"78987409" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-reso=
urce-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2021-9-=
15_4-56-53.png" data-base-url=3D"https://bluespace.fmeone.com" data-linked-=
resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"78=
985264" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"41" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D=
"" height=3D"245"></span></p>
<ul>
 <li>On getting the request in QuickService portal, AMS Engineer cross veri=
fies the user=E2=80=99s presence in Polarion by checking in&nbsp;<a class=
=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://polarion.gpdm.fmcglobal.net/polarion/#/h=
ome" rel=3D"nofollow">Home</a></li>
 <li>If user is new and doesn=E2=80=99t have account in Polarion, AMS Engin=
eer raises a request to create the user account in Polarion repository.</li=
>
 <li>To create the account in Polarion Repository, AMS Engineer raises a re=
quest to IT_Schweinfurt team using below URL:</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://jira-ext.=
fmc-ag.com/plugins/servlet/desk/portal/32/create/401" rel=3D"nofollow">IT-S=
W Portal</a></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>Example of Request:&nbsp;</strong>Once after the link is open, y=
ou will find all the below options and answers are highlighted.<br><br></p>
<ol>
 <li>
  <p>Um welche Windows Gruppen geht es? / Which Windows groups are we talki=
ng about?<br><br><strong><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">GG-DE-SCW-P=
olarion-ALM-Users<br><br></span></strong></p></li>
 <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><span><span class=3D"ui-provide=
r vf b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai=
 aj ak">Berechtigungen / Permissions<br><br><strong>Alle hinzuf=C3=BCgen or=
 Add All<br></strong><br></span></span></span></li>
 <li><span><span class=3D"ui-provider vf b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r =
s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak">F=C3=BCr wen sollen Berechtigun=
gen angepasst werden? / For whom should permissions be adjusted?<br><br><st=
rong>Anfrage f=C3=BCr einen anderen Benutzer or Request for another user<br=
><br></strong></span></span></li>
 <li><span><span class=3D"ui-provider vf b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r =
s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak">Kostenstelle / cost center<br><=
br><strong>DE01001032<br></strong><br></span></span></li>
 <li><span class=3D"ui-provider vf b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u =
v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak"><span class=3D"ui-provider vf b c d e=
 f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak">Besc=
hreibung / Description<br></span></span>
  <p style=3D"margin-left: 0.0px;"><strong><br>
     As agreed with IT Operations Schweinfurt, please add the following use=
r to group</strong></p>
  <p style=3D"margin-left: 0.0px;"><strong><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0=
.0px;">GG-DE-SCW-Polarion-ALM-Users:</span></strong></p>
  <p style=3D"margin-left: 0.0px;"><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><=
strong>FID:&nbsp;</strong><br><br></span></p></li>
</ol>
<ul>
 <li>Once the user is created in Polarion, AMS Engineer enable the user in =
production and provide the requested role/s (refer <span><a href=3D"#_Steps=
_to_Assign" rel=3D"nofollow">Section 3.3</a></span> Steps to Assign Project=
 Roles using Custom Web-UI).</li>
 <li>Once the Roles are provided, the AMS Engineer route the Request Form i=
n QDOK along with the training certificate for Archival.<br><br><br>
  <p style=3D"text-align: left;"><strong>Process to be followed by AMS Engi=
neer for NA User If User account is not present in polarion&nbsp;<br></stro=
ng>If user has account in NA AD, AMS Engineer will raise a request to get u=
ser added to&nbsp; <strong><span data-teams=3D"true">Polarion-Users<span>&n=
bsp;</span></span></strong><span data-teams=3D"true">group</span><strong><s=
pan data-teams=3D"true">.<br></span></strong> To create the account in pola=
rion Group. AMS Engineer will follow the below step:</p>
  <ol style=3D"text-align: left;">
   <li data-uuid=3D"75480c75-0bf7-4fa0-999f-52ba4251d085"><span data-teams=
=3D"true">AMS Engineer will raise a request to AD team using below URL: - <=
a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://fmcna.service-now.com/now/nav/ui/=
classic/params/target/incident.do%3Fsys_id%3D-1%26sysparm_query%3Dactive%3D=
true%26sysparm_stack%3Dincident_list.do%3Fsysparm_query%3Dactive%3Dtrue" re=
l=3D"nofollow">Incident-ServiceNow</a> fill below details&nbsp;</span>
    <ol style=3D"text-align: left;">
     <li data-uuid=3D"a70667e6-0ad5-4cf8-b770-e7c697842a53"><span data-team=
s=3D"true">Add description to ticket "Add User &lt;Username &gt;to &nbsp; <=
strong><span data-teams=3D"true">Polarion-Users AD<span>&nbsp;group&nbsp;</=
span></span></strong></span></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"cae5a16d-3c13-4206-9723-70443c13557c"><span data-team=
s=3D"true"><span data-teams=3D"true">Assign a group for services now ticket=
 as <strong>(<span style=3D"color:#333333;">DTI-INF-AD-L3)</span></strong><=
/span></span></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"d6d6d903-b1fd-43a3-b3b9-14f5cc89a63f">Once the user is =
added to Polarion group, AO Support engineer will enable the user in Polari=
on Production and provide the requested role/s.</li>
  </ol><br><strong>&nbsp;</strong></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Scena=
rio 2: Request For Admin Roles:</u></strong></p>
<p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p>
<p>If the User requests Global Admin role in Polarion, steps performed by A=
MS Engineer are:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Verify that the <span><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://qserv=
ice.intra.fmeone.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/create/283" rel=3D"nofo=
llow">Digital UACF</a></span> is correctly filled by Requestor and Approved=
 by the Approver on QuickService.</li>
</ul>
<p>Example:</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-w=
rapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-i=
mage" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"350" src=3D"64a77357a9fb92de7ce612782c0e=
186270f60f6b8d3261cec66f1dd358101d14" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachmen=
ts/78985264/image2021-9-15_4-57-20.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1=
631662043148&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-=
resource-id=3D"78987410" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-res=
ource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2021-9=
-15_4-57-20.png" data-base-url=3D"https://bluespace.fmeone.com" data-linked=
-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"7=
8985264" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"41" tabindex=3D"0" alt=
=3D"" height=3D"158"></span></p>
<ul>
 <li>Verify that the AMS Engineer has undergone internal training (provided=
 by the team) to ensure he is well acquainted with the process.</li>
 <li>If Yes, then route it to QDOK for approval from FMC Polarion Process O=
wner.</li>
 <li>Once the request is approved in QDOK, AO support engineer will create =
admin_FID account for the requestor and then provide the admin roles accord=
ingly.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p><strong><u>Scenario 3:&nbsp;Request to create Technical Users:</u></stro=
ng></p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If the request is to create Technic=
al Users, steps performed by AMS Engineer are:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Verify that the User Request Form is correctly filled.</li>
 <li>Confirm with the requestor if the Technical User has to be created in =
the Windows AD (it is usually in Windows AD)</li>
 <li>Route it to QDOK for approval from FMC Polarion Process Owner.</li>
 <li>Once the request is approved in QDOK, reach out to Michael Baunach to =
create the Technical User account for the requestor in Windows AD. Once the=
 user is created, provide the roles.</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><u>Scenario 4: Adding Roles in Projects:</u></strong></p>
<p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">An already existing Polarion user=
, requests access in other Projects in Polarion Production server.</span></=
p>
<ul>
 <li>The user raises a request in QuickService portal under =E2=80=9CDigita=
l User Account Request=E2=80=9D by clicking on the link(see screenshot).</l=
i>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-w=
rapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-i=
mage" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"350" src=3D"911648344a2e2946f97d762bc08f=
b54b234255087988d6c715af002e2eb82c8d" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachmen=
ts/78985264/image2021-9-15_4-57-53.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1=
631662075312&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-=
resource-id=3D"78987411" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-res=
ource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2021-9=
-15_4-57-53.png" data-base-url=3D"https://bluespace.fmeone.com" data-linked=
-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"7=
8985264" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"41" tabindex=3D"0" alt=
=3D"" height=3D"244"></span></p>
<ul>
 <li>The user fills the <span><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://qs=
ervice.intra.fresenius.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/create/283" rel=
=3D"nofollow">Digital UACF</a></span> (there are different forms for Single=
 User creation and Multiple User creation). User also needs to attach the r=
elevant Training certificate as per the requested Roles.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img =
class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"350" src=
=3D"1c3ee2bdf604cfc454a6ba57f10680bc9af6612de95d18d0dd0da48a33ee5a9c" data-=
image-src=3D"/download/attachments/78985264/image2021-9-15_4-58-13.png?vers=
ion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1631662095401&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-=
comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"78987412" data-linked-resour=
ce-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resou=
rce-default-alias=3D"image2021-9-15_4-58-13.png" data-base-url=3D"https://b=
luespace.fmeone.com" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-l=
inked-resource-container-id=3D"78985264" data-linked-resource-container-ver=
sion=3D"41" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"245"></span></p>
<p>The Training Certificate(s) needed as per the following roles are-</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Role</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Certificate(s)</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Project_user</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Read-only User Certificate</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Project_approver,<br><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project=
_assignable,<br></span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project_epm,<=
br></span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project_risk management,<b=
r></span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project_testmanager,<br></s=
pan><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project_changeapprover,<br></spa=
n><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Project_requirements_only</span></=
p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>General User Certificate OR<br><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px=
;">Polarion Change Management Certificate OR<br></span><span style=3D"lette=
r-spacing: 0.0px;">Certificates of Completion of =E2=80=93<br></span><span =
style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">GPDM Polarion Basics,<br></span><span styl=
e=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">GPDM Polarion Requirements Management,<br></sp=
an><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">GPDM Polarion Verification and Va=
lidation,<br></span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">GPDM Polarion Pr=
e-Production Defect Management,<br></span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.=
0px;">GPDM Polarion Design Requirement Traceability User Guide</span></p></=
td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Project_admin</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Project Admin certificate</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<ul>
 <li>AMS Engineer provides the request Roles in the Projects and informs th=
e user</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><u>Scenario 5:&nbsp;Removing Roles in Projects:</u></strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>An already existing Polarion user, requests removal of Roles from Pola=
rion Projects. The user raises a request in QuickService portal under =E2=
=80=9CDigital User Account Request=E2=80=9D by clicking on the link-- (see =
screenshot).</li>
</ul>
