<p><br></p>
<h3 id=3D"UserCreationinPolarion-Scenario6:ChangeinApplicationrolesinthetic=
ket"><u>Scenario 6: Change in Application roles in the ticket<br></u></h3>
<ul>
 <li>
  <p>If the User raises a UACF request for =E2=80=98X=E2=80=99 role in =E2=
=80=98Y=E2=80=99 project with an approver added in the ticket.</p>
  <p>Ex: PROJECT_USER role in 5008 Trunk project.<br><strong>Note:</strong>=
 <strong>An email notification should be sent to the approver to approve th=
e request.</strong><br><u><br></u></p></li>
 <li>
  <p>After sometimes, if the user requests in the same ticket, for addition=
al roles in the particular project.</p>Ex: PROJECT_USER, PROJECT_ASSIGNABLE=
, PROJECT_APPROVER, PROJECT_TESTMANAGER etc.. in the 5008 Trunk project.<br=
><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>No new additional email will be triggered t=
o the approver.</strong><br><br></li>
 <li>
  <p>To resolve this issue, remove the approver and again add the same pers=
on as the approver in the ticket to trigger <br>
    additional email with the correct details of the Application roles.</p>=
<br><br></li>
</ul>
<p>So that, approver can approve the correct details of Application roles.<=
br><br><br><strong>&nbsp;<u>Scenario 7: Request For Global_Read_Only Role:<=
/u></strong></p>
<p>If the User requests Global Read Only role in Polarion, steps performed =
by AMS Engineer are:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Verify that the <span><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://qserv=
ice.intra.fresenius.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/create/283" rel=3D"n=
ofollow">Digital UACF</a></span> is correctly filled by Requestor and Appro=
ved by the Approver on QuickService. <span style=3D"color:#000000;">The App=
rover of a Global Read only role only can only be a System Owner of the GPD=
M Polarion System.</span><br><br></li>
 <li>Once the request is approved in QuickService, AMS Engineer will provid=
e Global_Read_Only role for the user in production.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><span style=3D"color:#c25100;"><s=
trong>Note:</strong></span>&nbsp;To ensure that Users with Global_Read_Only=
 role can view content of GPDM Polarion projects a job (SetUserRoles.job) i=
s running everyday at 2 am CET to assign the Core_user role of the GPDM Pol=
arion projects also to the Global_ready_only accounts. Same holds true for =
removal of the Global_read_only role.</span></p>
<p><strong><u>Scenario 8: Pre-Requisites to be checked before giving access=
 on any Polarion project</u></strong></p>
<ul>
 <li><span>When a Polarion users requests access to any Polarion projects, =
AMS Engineer will check =E2=80=9Cdescription=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Ccontext=
=E2=80=9D thoroughly:</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>If user mentioned in the </span><strong><span>context,</span></s=
trong><span> that they need access in GPDM POLARION project and in </span><=
strong><span>description</span></strong><span> they mention any-another pro=
ject name, before proceeding further on this kind of request AMS Engineer n=
eeds to coordinate with user and to get confirm user want to access on GPDM=
 POLARION or not.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>Then AMS Engineer will provide access to user accordingly once a=
fter receiving confirmation from user.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style=3D"color:#c25100;"><strong>Note:</strong> </span><span>Don=
=E2=80=99t provide access on both projects which are mentioned in =E2=80=9C=
description=E2=80=9D and as well as =E2=80=9Ccontext=E2=80=9D, since someti=
mes users will mention a random project name/GPDM Polarion in context as th=
e target project won=E2=80=99t be available in context and target project w=
ill be mentioned in description or comment(sometimes)</span><span> .</span>=
</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><u><strong>Scenario 9:&nbsp;<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Onboa=
rding process for non-PLT users</span></strong></u></p>
<p><strong>Pre-Requisites to be checked by AMS Engineer for non-PLT:</stron=
g></p>
<ul>
 <li>User should be present in FME AD with entry in the =E2=80=98cn=E2=80=
=99 field=3D &lt;user FID&gt; or &nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;username&gt;.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Process to be followed by AMS Engineer for non-PLT:</strong></p>
<p>If user has account in FME AD, AMS Engineer will raise a request to get =
the user added to Polarion Group &lt; GG-DE-SCW-Polarion-ALM-Users&gt;.</p>
<p>To create the account in Polarion Group, AMS Engineer will follow the be=
low step:</p>
<ol>
 <li>AO Support engineer will raise a request to IT Schweinfurt team using =
below URL: &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://jira-ext.fmc-ag=
.com/plugins/servlet/desk/portal/32" rel=3D"nofollow">https://jira-ext.fmc-=
ag.com/plugins/servlet/desk/portal/32</a></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4986cd68-18a0-4818-81b6-21415a0ac726">Once the user is ad=
ded to Polarion group, AMS Engineer will enable the user in Polarion Produc=
tion and provide the requested role/s.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong><span><u>Scenario 10: <span data-teams=3D"true">Change of FID/Us=
erID</span></u></span></strong></p>
<p>If a user=E2=80=99s FID is changed and he raises a request to transfer t=
he roles/access from old FID to new UserID, the AMS Engineer has to validat=
e the below:</p>
<ul>
 <li>The user has raised a request in <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"ht=
tps://qservice.intra.fmeone.com/servicedesk/customer/portal/17/create/283" =
rel=3D"nofollow">quick service</a></li>
 <li>The user has filled the Digital UACF and selected Change FID option.</=
li>
 <li>The user has mentioned the old FID and the new FID (in which the roles=
/access has to be transferred).</li>
</ul>
<p>On receiving the request, the AMS Engineer follows the below process for=
 change the FID.</p>
<p><br></p>
<ul>
 <li>Step-1: Login to Polarion with your admin credentials.</li>
 <li>Step-2: Click on the gear icon on the top left and select administrati=
on in the drop down.</li>
 <li>Step-3: Select user management and select user.</li>
 <li>Step-4: Search for users old FID that is mentioned in the ticket in th=
e search box.</li>
 <li>step-5: &nbsp;New User ID need to be mapped with old FID [ how to map =
two accounts please check<a href=3D"https://bluespace.fmeone.com/display/KB=
GPTA/Polarion+Login+Issues" rel=3D"nofollow"> <u><strong>Scenario-</strong>=
</u></a><strong><u>4 in</u></strong>&nbsp;KB article</li>
 <li>Step-6: Click on Save to save the changes&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
